# A kick drum: press the button and it booms, the way the Roland TR-808's bass drum does.
#
# U1 is a resonator. In its feedback is a bridged-T: C1 and C2 in series from its output to its
# inverting input, R1 from between them to ground, and R2 across the pair. At one frequency,
# 1 / (2π · C · √(R1 · R2)), about 55 Hz, the network hands back almost all of what it is given, and
# U1 rings there when struck: a low sine dying away over about half a second, its quality
# ½ · √(R2 / R1), about 26, saying how slowly.
#
# The strike is the button. Pressing it puts BT's 9 V on CT, whose edge comes through D1 and RIN as a
# spike into U1's input: a thump with every frequency in it, which the resonator answers only at its
# own. D1 lets the press through and not the release, so one tap is one beat; RP and RQ empty CT
# again ready for the next.
#
# The speaker plays while the clock runs at a second a second; the status line says how fast the sound
# is being worked out, and whether it has ever had to stop and wait. Tap out a rhythm.

speed 1
start settled

battery   BP    40 9  40 12  9V
battery   BN    40 12 40 17  9V
ground          40 12
wire            20 9  40 9
wire            20 17 40 17

opamp     U1    20 12 TL072
wire            20 10 20 9
wire            20 14 20 17
wire            18 13 16 13
ground          16 13

# The bridged-T, from the output back to the inverting input.
wire            18 11 18 4
wire            22 12 24 12
wire            24 12 24 4
capacitor C2    18 4  21 4   100n
capacitor C1    21 4  24 4   100n
resistor  R1    21 4  21 7   560
ground          21 7
wire            18 4  18 1
resistor  R2    18 1  24 1   1.5meg
wire            24 1  24 4

# The strike.
battery   BT    4 8   4 12   9V
ground          4 12
button    S1    4 8   8 8
wire            8 8   10 8
resistor  RP    10 8  10 12  10k
ground          10 12
capacitor CT    10 8  12 8   10n
resistor  RQ    12 8  12 12  100k
ground          12 12
diode     D1    12 8  14 8
resistor  RIN   14 8  18 8   47k

# The speaker.
wire            24 12 28 12
resistor  RS    28 12 32 12  1k
speaker   SPK   32 12 32 14  8
ground          32 14

label     drum  26 12
meter     DRUM  28 12 32 14
